core wordpress theme (rmcc-theme)
only core features, nothing extra
all other feature branches be branched off & sync with this branch.

new 'latestcore' branch can keep the 'core' branch up-to-date & be used to later create the 'combined' branch
all other feature branches can stay synced with 'core', but 'combined' can be based off 'latestcore' & other features can be integrated into this manually
winmerge can be used to check the code changed between 'core' and any feature branch, so this feature can be pulled out and integrated into 'combined' via 'latestcore'
if we ever update 'core' we would need to update the core code then in all the feature branches, but this should be avoided now using the new 'latestcore' scheme
'core' from now on should only really be kept in this minimum viable & working state; instead 'latestcore' will be the branch to keep the core code fully up-to-date

'core' serves as the minimum-viable base for all individual branches
'latestcore' serves as the actual jumping off point for starting new blank (no features) projects. it also serves as the base for the 'combined' branch.